PanVK (Mesa 26.2.x), JM/Bifrost: direct vkCmdDrawIndexed with a CPU index range, opt-in.

Stock PanVK makes every vkCmdDrawIndexed on v6/v7 an indirect draw: write-value job, GPU min/max
index search to the end of the index buffer, indirect helper with a prefetch barrier, then vertex
and tiler jobs. On the RG DS's Mali-G52 that is ~0.4 ms of vertex-tiler time per draw (400 draws:
153 ms against GL's 6.4 ms).

PANVK_DIRECT_INDEXED=1: when the index buffer's memory is host-mapped, scan
[firstIndex, firstIndex + indexCount) on the CPU at record time (restart indices skipped) and emit
plain vertex + tiler jobs with vertex_range/raw_offset from the min/max and base_vertex_offset = -min,
as the indirect helper and Gallium panfrost do. The app must write the indices before recording the
draw. Without the variable, or for unmapped memory, the stock path runs unchanged.
PANVK_VARYING_SLAB_KB (default 64): varying pool slab size; direct draws allocate varyings per draw,
and 1024 keeps a 400-draw frame in one or two BOs (submit 1.0 -> 0.43 ms).

Measured in docs/TANUKI_VULKAN_PLAN.md (tools/tanuki3ds/vkspike).

